{"kind":"event","event_id":6308,"event_uid":"01M2MJ90GGCKS4ZMWPQF2RGW40","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":286,"issue_uid":"01M2MJ5ZVQH794D9HXYBWB9GK5","issue_short_id":"9gk5","actor":"impl:1@run-21","hlc_physical_ms":1789544137232,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"c628aa17411dd18923bfd7cfcf74cfb71e31f4b51864eacbc80aab0bac318e31","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2MJ90GF8XWH07M75Y78EQ45","author":"impl:1@run-21","body":"Task 1 approach: add `pinned: {type: 'boolean'}` (no default) to TODO_CELLS in client/src/storeData.ts so both todos and trash carry it; add `pinTodo(store, id, pinned)` mirroring setTodoCompleted with the two edges (return when !hasRow; delCell on false, setPartialRow on true). TodoItem gets data-pinned on both branches, a ' pinned' class suffix, and a plain <button id={`pin-${rowId}`} type=\"button\"> placed AFTER Delete so '.todoItem button' still clicks Delete. Re-export pinTodo through Store.tsx. .gitignore gains 'state-exams/posted/'. Expected file state-exams/expected/two-todos-second-pinned.json written as one line. The exam at tests/state-exams/pin-todo.test.ts is the peer's — I write no test file.","created_at":"2026-09-16T07:35:37.231065201Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T07:35:37.232Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":6322,"event_uid":"01M2MJAEPAQ1H608QJJM2DMEB2","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":286,"issue_uid":"01M2MJ5ZVQH794D9HXYBWB9GK5","issue_short_id":"9gk5","actor":"exam:1@run-21","hlc_physical_ms":1789544184522,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"7bbdf38d7bb6dc3715de964ecec910ed0bb76fbe072c993e78343da54414f042","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2MJAEP9XB6WXEGCDSC8SVRV","author":"exam:1@run-21","body":"examiner: writing tests/state-exams/pin-todo.test.ts as nine legs against M1-M7, on the shape delete-to-trash.test.ts already uses — one module-level stateExam for leg (a) (seed two-open-todos.json, click #pin-1, expected two-todos-second-pinned.json, the five view entries and the absent-pinned mutant, all verbatim from the leg), and every other leg an ordinary bun:test block beside it. The store module is reached through one namespace import (import * as sd) so that an absent pinTodo is one red leg rather than a load error for the whole file; every fixture read happens inside a test body, because the linter's capture child imports this file with stateExam and bun:test stubbed out. Measured at BASE: renderStatic over M1's literal does not throw — the schema simply drops the unknown pinned cell — so leg (f) goes red on the missing data-pinned attribute and the missing pin buttons, not on an exception; the linter's four test files are 23 pass in 13.7s.","created_at":"2026-09-16T07:36:24.521425302Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-16T07:36:24.522Z"}
